"paper"],"description_full":"Accenture plc provides consulting and managed services in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. It offers artificial intelligence and data; cloud consulting; cybersecurity consulting; digital engineering and manufacturing; ecosystem partners; emerging technology; finance and risk management consulting; infrastructure and capital projects; digital learning; supply chain consulting; technology consulting; sustainability consulting; and metaverse solutions, as well as customer services. The company also provides proprietary assets and platforms, such as GenWizard, SynOps and reinvention.AI to clients. It serves aerospace and defense, automotive, banking, capital markets, chemicals, communications and media, consumer goods and services, energy, health, high tech, industrial, insurance, life sciences, natural resources, private equity, public service, retail, software and platforms, travel, and utilities industries. Accenture plc was founded in 1951 and is based in Dublin, Ireland.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Julie T. Spellman Sweet J.D. | CEO & Chairman | Age 58 | Compensation: $6.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 814K people. Revenue per employee of $91K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $14K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 74\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Accenture plc is a large-cap technology business with a $130.7B market cap on $74.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 36% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 26-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $11.6B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.48\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 38\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 8.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (77% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.231},{"text":"Significant goodwill (36% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 19.3% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 48% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 37% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","20 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Technology peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Accenture PLC $ACN Holdings Raised by Ieq Capital LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/accenture-plc-acn-holdings-raised-by-ieq-capital-llc.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795183608.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"13,422 Accenture PLC $ACN Shares Purchased by Private Wealth Asset Management LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/13422-accenture-plc-acn-shares-purchased-by-private-wealth-asset-management-llc.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795178816.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.966,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"7,082 Accenture PLC $ACN Shares Bought by Intech Investment Management LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/7082-accenture-plc-acn-shares-bought-by-intech-investment-management-llc.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795176048.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Accenture (NYSE:ACN) Share Price Crosses Below 50-Day Movin